TYPES.md §5.2 (E3304), §1, DECISIONS 209: a case check calling a method broken by an identifier
map key is broken, so its variant is too, and the let typed by it: the check never runs.
-- features/mail/mail.canon --
/// Mails.
package features.mail

/// A mail.
variant Mail {
  /// A letter.
  letter {
    /// Its subject.
    subject: String
    /// Whether it is sent on a holiday.
    fn isHoliday() -> Bool {
      let zzMap: {String: Int} = { a: 1 }
      return zzMap == {}
    }
    warn isHoliday() else "a holiday mail usually carries penya"
  }
}

/// The mails.
let mails: [Mail] = [letter { subject: "Spring cleaning" }]
